# bs0.hex - Canonical encoding of minimal L* instance
# Instance: φ₀ = (x₁ ∨ x₂ ∨ x₃), n_core=3, m=1
# Encoding follows Appendix D.5.2 specification
#
# To extract raw bytes: grep -v '^#' bs0.hex | xxd -r -p > bs0.bin
#
# === F1: Header "4:3:1:" ===
# len=4, content="3:1:" → n_core=3, m=1
343a333a313a
# === F2: DAG Adjacency "5:1:0::" ===
# len=5, content="1:0::" → 1 node, node 0 has 0 parents
353a313a303a3a
# === F3: Emergence Matrices "6:3:3:" + matrix bytes ===
# len=6, R₀=3, cols=3
# H₀ = I₃ → row-major bits: 1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1
# MSB-first packing: 10001000 10000000 = 0x88 0x80
363a333a333a8880
# === F4: Salt Table "32:" + 8 entries of form "2:<2 bytes>" (u=0..7) ===
33323a
323aa73c
323a5b91
323ae24f
323a18d6
323ac37a
323a6d05
323af4b8
323a29e3
# === F5: Initial Seed "16:" + 16 bytes (128-bit, big-endian, zero-padded) ===
31363a
00000000000000000000000000004a2f
# === F6: Gate Requirements "1:" + bits (one bit, packed MSB-first) ===
# GREQ₀ = 1 → bit 7 set → 0x80
313a80
# === F7: Masked Literal Table "2:" + literal bits ===
# b = ⌈log₂ 3⌉ + 1 = 3 bits per literal
# MINIMAL INSTANCE: mask R = 0 (all zeros), so E = enc(lit) directly
# enc(x₁)=001, enc(x₂)=010, enc(x₃)=011 (bit[2]=polarity=0, bits[1:0]=var_id)
# Concatenated: 001 010 011 = 9 bits
# MSB-first packing: 00101001 10000000 = 0x29 0x80
323a2980
